<section class="spec" id="product">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal" style="max-width:640px;margin-bottom:34px">
      <span class="kicker">At the desk, and in the office</span>
      <h2 class="title">The week <span class="h-mark">arrives ready<svg class="scribble-under" viewBox="0 0 300 16" aria-hidden="true"><path style="--len:340" d="M3 11 C 52 4, 104 14, 152 8 C 200 2, 250 12, 297 6"/></svg><svg class="scribble-spark" viewBox="0 0 34 34" aria-hidden="true"><path style="--len:120" d="M17 3 V13 M17 21 V31 M3 17 H13 M21 17 H31 M7 7 L12 12 M22 22 L27 27 M27 7 L22 12 M12 22 L7 27"/></svg></span></h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Everything a teaching week asks for, prepared before it is asked — you review, adjust and approve.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- feature folder-cards, in two rooms: the teacher's desk and the school office -->
    <div class="fgroup-head reveal">
      <h3>At the teacher's desk</h3>
      <p>Everything ready before the lesson is.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid fg-desk">

      <article id="teaching-notes" class="fcard reveal" style="--tint:var(--orange)">
        <span class="fcard-kicker">Teaching notes &amp; copilot</span>
        <h3>Ready for the chapter before you are</h3>
        <p>Ask the copilot for class notes you can actually teach with, or write and paste your own in the note editor — everything lands in your library.</p>
        <div class="fcard-visual">
          <div class="feed-item"><i>T</i><div><b>"Notes for Ch 4, class VIII"</b>Draft ready to edit</div></div>
          <div class="feed-item"><i>T</i><div><b>"Simpler, for the second section"</b>Rewritten at VII&#8209;B level</div></div>
          <div class="feed-item"><i>T</i><div><b>"Add a board-style ray diagram"</b>Added to the note</div></div>
          <div class="feed-item"><i>&#9998;</i><div><b>Saved to your library</b>Optics &middot; Ch 4 &middot; two versions</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article id="question-papers" class="fcard reveal" style="--tint:var(--violet)">
        <span class="fcard-kicker">Homework &amp; assignments</span>
        <h3>Set in a minute, and home already knows</h3>
        <p>Homework drafted for what you taught today. The moment you assign it, parents are notified — so it actually gets done at home.</p>
        <div class="fcard-visual">
          <div class="q-line"><b style="color:var(--violet)">HW</b>Ch 5 &middot; Q1&ndash;4 &middot; due Thursday<span>&#10003;</span></div>
          <div class="q-line"><b style="color:var(--violet)">&#9993;</b>44 parents notified &middot; VII&#8209;B<span>&#10003;</span></div>
          <div class="q-line"><b style="color:var(--violet)">&#10003;</b>38 submitted by Wednesday night<span></span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article id="shared-library" class="fcard reveal" style="--tint:var(--yellow)">
        <span class="fcard-kicker">Shared library</span>
        <h3>One teacher's notes, every teacher's shelf</h3>
        <p>Your repository is private by default. Share a note and it's visible to everyone on your school's email — any class, any department.</p>
        <div class="fcard-visual">
          <div class="lib-grid">
            <figure><div class="np np-ruled"></div><figcaption>Ch 4 &middot; Light <i>R.&#8202;Nair</i></figcaption></figure>
